<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ala Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1691">1691</a>–<a href="/years/1765">1765</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Baba Ala Singh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ala Singh was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> chief of the Phulkian family and the founder of Patiala State. From the 1720s he built up power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> and founded the fort of Patiala in 1763. He survived by balancing between the Sikh misls and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a>, who recognised him as a ruler.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ala-singh.jpg" alt="Ala Singh" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Painting_of_Ala_Singh_of_Patiala_in_tondo,_Pahari_School,_ca.1880.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
